This is a new format sample. 

```
{
  "draft": 5,
  "header_table_size": 4096,
  "context": "request",
  "cases": [
    {
      "wire": "gocDiPRGbWkS0nF3hw==",
      "headers": [
        [ ":method", "GET" ],
        [ ":scheme", "http" ],
        [ ":authority", "yahoo.co.jp" ],
        [ ":path", "/" ]
      ]
    },
    .....
  ]
}
```

@kazu-yamamoto @tatsuhiro-t @Jxck 
If you have any point, please feedback.

@Jxck @summerwind and I discussed this:
- Keep the name of "header_table_size"
- It means that SETTINGS_HEADER_TABLE_SIZE is sent and ACKed just before this case
- No requirement to add this field to the first case. If omitted, 4,096 is used.

@tatsuhiro-t what do you think?
